00:55:22.000 --> 00:55:22.999
There was a mission?

00:55:23.000 --> 00:55:24.999
There's something I want to hear.

00:55:25.000 --> 00:55:26.999
Hmm.

00:55:27.000 --> 00:55:28.999
Get it in one guess

00:55:29.000 --> 00:55:30.999
and I'll buy you something good.

00:55:31.000 --> 00:55:33.999
Guess what we'll eat?

00:55:34.000 --> 00:55:34.999
Yep.

00:55:35.000 --> 00:55:36.999
What am I guessing? — You've got to say

00:55:37.000 --> 00:55:38.999
what I want to hear. Then I'll buy you

00:55:39.000 --> 00:55:41.999
something good. — Okay, okay.

00:55:42.000 --> 00:55:43.999
I'll try. — Go.

00:55:44.000 --> 00:55:45.999
What's the question?

00:55:46.000 --> 00:55:48.999
You just have to say what I want to hear,

00:55:49.000 --> 00:55:49.999
hyung.

00:55:50.000 --> 00:55:52.999
Okay, but what do you

00:55:53.000 --> 00:55:53.999
want to hear?

00:55:54.000 --> 00:55:56.999
That's what you have to guess.

00:55:57.000 --> 00:55:58.999
How can I guess when you haven't

00:55:59.000 --> 00:56:01.999
told me anything? — I gave you a hint!

00:56:02.000 --> 00:56:02.999
A hint?

00:56:03.000 --> 00:56:04.999
Yep.

00:56:05.000 --> 00:56:07.999
Give me one more.

00:56:08.000 --> 00:56:13.999
It's got something to do with food.

00:56:14.000 --> 00:56:15.999
Food...

00:56:16.000 --> 00:56:18.999
Your hyung will buy you something good.

00:56:19.000 --> 00:56:19.999
I love you.

00:56:20.000 --> 00:56:21.999
Ding-dong!

00:56:22.000 --> 00:56:25.999
Congratulations. Your affection meter

00:56:26.000 --> 00:56:27.999
is maxed out. That's a lot of affection!

00:56:28.000 --> 00:56:28.999
Oh, thank you.

00:56:29.000 --> 00:56:31.999
Ja, Bamby, you're not watching right now?

00:56:32.000 --> 00:56:32.999
You're just on the phone?

00:56:33.000 --> 00:56:34.999
— Right. — Wow.

00:56:35.000 --> 00:56:36.999
How did you get it in one?

00:56:37.000 --> 00:56:37.999
That gave me goosebumps.

00:56:38.000 --> 00:56:38.999
I got it right away.

00:56:39.000 --> 00:56:40.999
The hair on my whole body stood up,

00:56:41.000 --> 00:56:41.999
just like Noah-hyung.

00:56:42.000 --> 00:56:43.999
We've known each other a long time,

00:56:44.000 --> 00:56:44.999
after all.

00:56:45.000 --> 00:56:45.999
That's true.

00:56:46.000 --> 00:56:47.999
It might've been a little surprising.

00:56:48.000 --> 00:56:48.999
It was.

00:56:49.000 --> 00:56:49.999
Yeah.

00:56:50.000 --> 00:56:51.999
Thanks so much for taking

00:56:52.000 --> 00:56:53.999
the time to call.

00:56:54.000 --> 00:56:56.999
— Of course. — We see each other every
day,

00:56:57.000 --> 00:56:59.999
so we'll just

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:01.999
see each other as usual. Say a few words

00:57:02.000 --> 00:57:03.999
to PLLI,

00:57:04.000 --> 00:57:05.999
then you can get back to what you were
doing.

00:57:06.000 --> 00:57:07.999
Ja, PLLI, it's gotten

00:57:08.000 --> 00:57:09.999
quite chilly today.

00:57:10.000 --> 00:57:12.999
November, December... Yes, winter weather

00:57:13.000 --> 00:57:15.999
is back. And in winter,

00:57:16.000 --> 00:57:19.999
you've got to be careful not to catch a
cold.

00:57:20.000 --> 00:57:21.999
So instead of an iced Americano,

00:57:22.000 --> 00:57:23.999
I'd recommend

00:57:24.000 --> 00:57:25.999
a hot one. Always dress

00:57:26.000 --> 00:57:27.999
warmly,

00:57:28.000 --> 00:57:30.999
and don't catch a cold.

00:57:31.000 --> 00:57:32.999
That's your mission.

00:57:33.000 --> 00:57:35.999
Hyung, is this today's horoscope

00:57:36.000 --> 00:57:36.999
