01:09:01.000 --> 01:09:02.999
one notch for oppa, three for cuteness,

01:09:03.000 --> 01:09:05.999
and three for happiness. If I can't fill
them all,

01:09:06.000 --> 01:09:06.999
I can't get back

01:09:07.000 --> 01:09:08.999
to Asterum. PLLI,

01:09:09.000 --> 01:09:11.999
we're running out of time,

01:09:12.000 --> 01:09:16.999
so let's fill those meters fast.

01:09:17.000 --> 01:09:18.999
Ja.

01:09:19.000 --> 01:09:21.999
Time for some oppa talk.

01:09:22.000 --> 01:09:26.999
I'll sit down.

01:09:27.000 --> 01:09:27.999
Some of you are even saying

01:09:28.000 --> 01:09:30.999
I look like an oppa just sitting here.

01:09:31.000 --> 01:09:33.999
You might not know this, but

01:09:34.000 --> 01:09:35.999
more people see me as an oppa

01:09:36.000 --> 01:09:37.999
than you'd think.

01:09:38.000 --> 01:09:39.999
Not that I'm thrilled to say it myself,

01:09:40.000 --> 01:09:43.999
but anyway...

01:09:44.000 --> 01:09:46.999
Now...

01:09:47.000 --> 01:09:49.999
Here's a little TMI.

01:09:50.000 --> 01:09:52.999
Early yesterday morning,

01:09:53.000 --> 01:09:54.999
all of a sudden, a mosquito

01:09:55.000 --> 01:09:57.999
started buzzing around.

01:09:58.000 --> 01:09:59.999
I switched on the light

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:01.999
and kept breathing. Here's my tip:

01:10:02.000 --> 01:10:05.999
keep breathing

01:10:06.000 --> 01:10:08.999
like this, right?

01:10:09.000 --> 01:10:10.999
It'll fly right in front of you. Then grab
it.

01:10:11.000 --> 01:10:14.999
I grabbed it, and sure enough...

01:10:15.000 --> 01:10:18.999
and there was blood, just like that.

01:10:19.000 --> 01:10:21.999
They say mosquitoes are drawn to carbon
dioxide.

01:10:22.000 --> 01:10:24.999
Apparently there's a whole method:

01:10:25.000 --> 01:10:27.999
turn on your flashlight in a dark room,

01:10:28.000 --> 01:10:30.999
and it'll come right up to you.

01:10:31.000 --> 01:10:32.999
It's a little hard to catch like that,

01:10:33.000 --> 01:10:35.999
so just leave the lights on. And if

01:10:36.000 --> 01:10:37.999
it's already bitten you, it'll fly lower,

01:10:38.000 --> 01:10:41.999
because it's heavier. So...

01:10:42.000 --> 01:10:43.999
That's my tip. So yesterday,

01:10:44.000 --> 01:10:47.999
I caught that mosquito, was up a little
longer,

01:10:48.000 --> 01:10:50.999
then fell asleep.

01:10:51.000 --> 01:10:53.999
Aw, thanks for the head pats.

01:10:54.000 --> 01:10:55.999
I don't know whose hand that is,

01:10:56.000 --> 01:10:57.999
but I'll think of it as PLLI's.

01:10:58.000 --> 01:11:01.999
Ja, like I said earlier,

01:11:02.000 --> 01:11:03.999
some of you might've missed it.

01:11:04.000 --> 01:11:05.999
You might be thinking,

01:11:06.000 --> 01:11:07.999
“Hamin's diction isn't great,”

01:11:08.000 --> 01:11:09.999
if you just joined. So

01:11:10.000 --> 01:11:12.999
one last time: I had one,

01:11:13.000 --> 01:11:15.999
two, three, and now the fourth and final

01:11:16.000 --> 01:11:18.999
wisdom tooth taken out.

01:11:19.000 --> 01:11:21.999
The last one. It's gone.

01:11:22.000 --> 01:11:23.999
Wow.

01:11:24.000 --> 01:11:26.999
Oh, pulling wisdom teeth makes you an
oppa?

01:11:27.000 --> 01:11:29.999
If only I'd saved the other three

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:31.999
and pulled them all at once,

01:11:32.000 --> 01:11:34.999
the meter would've shot up.

01:11:35.000 --> 01:11:37.999
Ja, anyway, now I have

01:11:38.000 --> 01:11:43.999
the teeth of a true adult.

01:11:44.000 --> 01:11:45.999
Anyway, PLLI, I always say this:

01:11:46.000 --> 01:11:48.999
whether Hamin's an oppa

01:11:49.000 --> 01:11:51.999
or a baby, isn't loving Hamin

01:11:52.000 --> 01:11:54.999
the right answer?

01:11:55.000 --> 01:11:57.999
When I look more like an oppa,

01:11:58.000 --> 01:11:59.999
enjoy that. When I look like a baby,

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:02.999
enjoy that too. Isn't that nice?

01:12:03.000 --> 01:12:03.999
Like this version of Hamin

01:12:04.000 --> 01:12:06.999
and that version too. Right?

01:12:07.000 --> 01:12:10.999
I hope you'll like both.

01:12:11.000 --> 01:12:11.999
Ja.

01:12:12.000 --> 01:12:13.999
“Adult teeth? Wasn't it a baby tooth?”

01:12:14.000 --> 01:12:16.999
Very childish of you.

01:12:17.000 --> 01:12:17.999
Ja.

01:12:18.000 --> 01:12:21.999
In that case...

01:12:22.000 --> 01:12:25.999
I've still got lots prepared.

01:12:26.000 --> 01:12:27.999
Curious, aren't you?

01:12:28.000 --> 01:12:29.999
Are you curious?

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:32.999
Curious? That'll be 500 won.

01:12:33.000 --> 01:12:34.999
Honestly, did anyone get that joke?

01:12:35.000 --> 01:12:36.999
Anyone?

01:12:37.000 --> 01:12:40.999
Hmm. I saw that. I can see everything.

01:12:41.000 --> 01:12:41.999
I'll take a sip of water.

01:12:42.000 --> 01:12:47.999
This is embarrassing.

01:12:48.000 --> 01:12:49.999
The PLLI Room's really well decorated.

01:12:50.000 --> 01:12:52.999
There's a dartboard and a telescope,

01:12:53.000 --> 01:12:54.999
too.

01:12:55.000 --> 01:12:57.999
I could live here. Is that

01:12:58.000 --> 01:13:01.999
a mobile up there?

01:13:02.000 --> 01:13:05.999
Oh, a telescope. Okay.

01:13:06.000 --> 01:13:09.999
There's a couch. It's cozy here.

01:13:10.000 --> 01:13:10.999
Someone actually sent 500 won.

01:13:11.000 --> 01:13:14.999
Look at that.

01:13:15.000 --> 01:13:16.999
I'm going to take some questions

01:13:17.000 --> 01:13:18.999
from PLLI

01:13:19.000 --> 01:13:22.999
and try to answer them. Someone asked

01:13:23.000 --> 01:13:24.999
if I'm sad there's only one date

01:13:25.000 --> 01:13:25.999
left

01:13:26.000 --> 01:13:29.999
on the world tour.

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:32.999
Well, time really does fly.

01:13:33.000 --> 01:13:35.999
At every single show,

01:13:36.000 --> 01:13:38.999
I just focused on that day.

01:13:39.000 --> 01:13:41.999
And just like that,

01:13:42.000 --> 01:13:45.999
there's only one show left.

01:13:46.000 --> 01:13:47.999
But I'm actually feeling pretty good.

01:13:48.000 --> 01:13:50.999
Relieved, even?

01:13:51.000 --> 01:13:54.999
I got to see PLLI laugh and cry,

01:13:55.000 --> 01:13:56.999
and it gave me so much energy.

01:13:57.000 --> 01:13:58.999
I feel really recharged now,

01:13:59.000 --> 01:14:01.999
so when we get to do concerts again,

01:14:02.000 --> 01:14:03.999
I think I'll be able to give even more.

01:14:04.000 --> 01:14:08.999
And we'll finish this one well, too.

01:14:09.000 --> 01:14:11.999
Ah, a serious...

01:14:12.000 --> 01:14:13.999
Oh, serious talk makes the oppa meter go
up?

01:14:14.000 --> 01:14:23.999
Love you!

01:14:24.000 --> 01:14:26.999
That went down the wrong way.

01:14:27.000 --> 01:14:29.999
This is an unusual stream.

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:31.999
Ah, sorry.

01:14:32.000 --> 01:14:34.999
Ja, someone asks about an encore concert.

01:14:35.000 --> 01:14:37.999
An encore? Well...

01:14:38.000 --> 01:14:40.999
First I need to get out of the PLLI Room

01:14:41.000 --> 01:14:42.999
before I can do an encore or anything.

01:14:43.000 --> 01:14:44.999
Today's what matters, everyone.

01:14:45.000 --> 01:14:47.999
You know that, right?

01:14:48.000 --> 01:14:50.999
Love you. Now raise me

01:14:51.000 --> 01:14:54.999
with your love.

01:14:55.000 --> 01:14:56.999
Ja, there's no tour stop this weekend,

01:14:57.000 --> 01:14:58.999
so someone asked what I'm planning

01:14:59.000 --> 01:15:01.999
to do with the time.

01:15:02.000 --> 01:15:03.999
For me...

01:15:04.000 --> 01:15:04.999
Weekends...

01:15:05.000 --> 01:15:07.999
How do I put it?

01:15:08.000 --> 01:15:09.999
Are we freelancers?

01:15:10.000 --> 01:15:12.999
People with this kind of job

01:15:13.000 --> 01:15:15.999
lose track of the days. Weekdays

01:15:16.000 --> 01:15:19.999
and weekends feel the same. When there's
time,

01:15:20.000 --> 01:15:21.999
I'll take a little for myself,

01:15:22.000 --> 01:15:24.999
study if there's something

01:15:25.000 --> 01:15:28.999
I need to study, or stream something

01:15:29.000 --> 01:15:31.999
I've been wanting to watch.

01:15:32.000 --> 01:15:35.999
I'll chat with PLLI, do a bit of this and
that.

01:15:36.000 --> 01:15:38.999
That's about it.

01:15:39.000 --> 01:15:41.999
I've got no sense of what day it is.

01:15:42.000 --> 01:15:43.999
So when I'm off, I just rest these days.

01:15:44.000 --> 01:15:45.999
“Are you working out lately?”

01:15:46.000 --> 01:15:48.999
A little, nothing too intense

01:15:49.000 --> 01:15:50.999
at the moment.

01:15:51.000 --> 01:15:52.999
During the tour, we dance so much.

01:15:53.000 --> 01:15:55.999
I've already built up my stamina,

01:15:56.000 --> 01:15:58.999
and pushing it more might just wear me
down.

01:15:59.000 --> 01:16:00.999
So I haven't been working out

01:16:01.000 --> 01:16:02.999
that hard.

01:16:03.000 --> 01:16:06.999
I just stretch when I get up at home

01:16:07.000 --> 01:16:10.999
and use a foam roller.

01:16:11.000 --> 01:16:14.999
I try to get my hips aligned,

01:16:15.000 --> 01:16:16.999
that sort of thing. So

01:16:17.000 --> 01:16:18.999
that's what you wanted to know.

01:16:19.000 --> 01:16:20.999
What do you do on weekends, PLLI?

01:16:21.000 --> 01:16:23.999
Do you rest?

01:16:24.000 --> 01:16:28.999
Everyone spends their days differently.

01:16:29.000 --> 01:16:31.999
Ah, you say I'm smart about taking care of
myself.

01:16:32.000 --> 01:16:35.999
Right. You've got to be smart about it.

01:16:36.000 --> 01:16:38.999
Smart, smart.

01:16:39.000 --> 01:16:40.999
Hmm.

01:16:41.000 --> 01:16:42.999
Oh, the meter goes up a bit

01:16:43.000 --> 01:16:44.999
while we chat.

01:16:45.000 --> 01:16:48.999
There it goes.

01:16:49.000 --> 01:16:50.999
Oh!

01:16:51.000 --> 01:16:52.999
“Thinking about PLAVE.”

01:16:53.000 --> 01:16:54.999
Of course.

01:16:55.000 --> 01:16:57.999
Some of you are thinking about Hamin, too.

01:16:58.000 --> 01:17:00.999
Right.

01:17:01.000 --> 01:17:04.999
Some of you are working, too.

01:17:05.000 --> 01:17:06.999
PLLI really do have

01:17:07.000 --> 01:17:09.999
an incredible range of jobs.

01:17:10.000 --> 01:17:13.999
We talked about this on a previous live.

01:17:14.000 --> 01:17:14.999
You do all kinds of work, and

01:17:15.000 --> 01:17:18.999
I really respect that. Every job

01:17:19.000 --> 01:17:21.999
has its own challenges.

01:17:22.000 --> 01:17:23.999
You're all doing your best,

01:17:24.000 --> 01:17:27.999
and I'll always

01:17:28.000 --> 01:17:33.999
be cheering you on.

01:17:34.000 --> 01:17:36.999
Someone's asking for

01:17:37.000 --> 01:17:38.999
today's TMI.

01:17:39.000 --> 01:17:41.999
Well, the mosquito story

01:17:42.000 --> 01:17:43.999
was my TMI.

01:17:44.000 --> 01:17:46.999
Oh, today...

01:17:47.000 --> 01:17:48.999
I vacuumed before I came.

01:17:49.000 --> 01:17:51.999
Dust had piled up,

01:17:52.000 --> 01:17:54.999
so I vacuumed all the corners.

01:17:55.000 --> 01:17:59.999
I got up and warmed up my voice...

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:02.999
[Hamin starts singing]

01:18:03.000 --> 01:18:06.999
[Singing continues]

01:18:07.000 --> 01:18:09.999
[Singing continues]

01:18:10.000 --> 01:18:15.999
[Singing continues]

01:18:16.000 --> 01:18:18.999
[Singing continues]

01:18:19.000 --> 01:18:22.999
[Singing trails off]

01:18:23.000 --> 01:18:25.999
Oh, I forgot to air the room out.

01:18:26.000 --> 01:18:29.999
[Briefly resumes singing]

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:30.999
Oh, a leak! How'd that happen?

01:18:31.000 --> 01:18:32.999
That's what I'm like

01:18:33.000 --> 01:18:34.999
at home.

01:18:35.000 --> 01:18:38.999
I'm pretty ordinary, too.

01:18:39.000 --> 01:18:41.999
What did I eat?

01:18:42.000 --> 01:18:43.999
Hmm.

01:18:44.000 --> 01:18:47.999
I was keeping that a secret.

01:18:48.000 --> 01:18:53.999
Should I tell you since it's my birthday
stream?

01:18:54.000 --> 01:18:57.999
I cooked instant noodles at home.

01:18:58.000 --> 01:19:01.999
But when I ate them,

01:19:02.000 --> 01:19:05.999
they didn't taste like they used to.

01:19:06.000 --> 01:19:08.999
I was so upset. Had they gone bad?

01:19:09.000 --> 01:19:10.999
Did they change the recipe? I checked the
packet.

01:19:11.000 --> 01:19:14.999
Turns out the date on it was

01:19:15.000 --> 01:19:16.999
sometime in June.

01:19:17.000 --> 01:19:18.999
Do they taste different after that date?

01:19:19.000 --> 01:19:21.999
Or is this why my sense of taste

01:19:22.000 --> 01:19:24.999
is going?

01:19:25.000 --> 01:19:26.999
Anyway, I still

01:19:27.000 --> 01:19:28.999
enjoyed them.

01:19:29.000 --> 01:19:30.999
So I had that,

01:19:31.000 --> 01:19:34.999
then before the stream,

01:19:35.000 --> 01:19:37.999
I had sushi.

01:19:38.000 --> 01:19:41.999
Sushi's such an easy meal.

01:19:42.000 --> 01:19:44.999
What's my favorite kind?

01:19:45.000 --> 01:19:47.999
I can't tell you that.

01:19:48.000 --> 01:19:49.999
I can tell you

01:19:50.000 --> 01:19:52.999
if the meter goes up.

01:19:53.000 --> 01:19:54.999
Yep.

01:19:55.000 --> 01:19:58.999
Personally, I'm a big fan

01:19:59.000 --> 01:20:00.999
of flame-seared sushi.

01:20:01.000 --> 01:20:02.999
What is that? It's not sushi that's on
fire.

01:20:03.000 --> 01:20:05.999
You sear it with a blowtorch.

01:20:06.000 --> 01:20:11.999
Like seared salmon,

01:20:12.000 --> 01:20:14.999
or eel, that kind of thing.

01:20:15.000 --> 01:20:17.999
I love those. As for the order I eat them
in,

01:20:18.000 --> 01:20:20.999
my absolute favorites are

01:20:21.000 --> 01:20:23.999
seared salmon and eel.

01:20:24.000 --> 01:20:26.999
Both of them. You know how some people

01:20:27.000 --> 01:20:28.999
decide what order to eat things in?

01:20:29.000 --> 01:20:31.999
I don't just eat whatever's in front of
me.

01:20:32.000 --> 01:20:34.999
I always start with seared salmon

01:20:35.000 --> 01:20:38.999
and save the eel

01:20:39.000 --> 01:20:40.999
for last.

01:20:41.000 --> 01:20:43.999
Hmm. Someone asks,

01:20:44.000 --> 01:20:46.999
“If PLLI asked, would you give them

01:20:47.000 --> 01:20:48.999
both the salmon and the eel?”

01:20:49.000 --> 01:20:52.999
Yellowtail's gotten

01:20:53.000 --> 01:20:54.999
so expensive lately, so

01:20:55.000 --> 01:20:58.999
I'd have to think about that.
Rock-paper-scissors?

01:20:59.000 --> 01:21:01.999
I'm kidding. Of course I'd give them to
you.

01:21:02.000 --> 01:21:04.999
You can have them all. I'll just go home

01:21:05.000 --> 01:21:07.999
and eat my expired noodles.

01:21:08.000 --> 01:21:10.999
Yep.

01:21:11.000 --> 01:21:12.999
Just kidding.

01:21:13.000 --> 01:21:14.999
PLLI, I hope you get to eat

01:21:15.000 --> 01:21:17.999
lots of good food.

01:21:18.000 --> 01:21:19.999
But I'm seriously hungry now. What do I
do?

01:21:20.000 --> 01:21:21.999
Maybe I was too nervous today.

01:21:22.000 --> 01:21:23.999
How's the stream been? Were those

01:21:24.000 --> 01:21:25.999
action moves okay earlier? We really

01:21:26.000 --> 01:21:28.999
rehearsed them a lot,

01:21:29.000 --> 01:21:32.999
so I hope they looked good.

01:21:33.000 --> 01:21:35.999
I put a lot of work into it.

01:21:36.000 --> 01:21:37.999
Ja, anyway, I'll talk about that

01:21:38.000 --> 01:21:40.999
later.

01:21:41.000 --> 01:21:42.999
Ja, shall we loosen up a little?

01:21:43.000 --> 01:21:45.999
You've been sitting a long time.

01:21:46.000 --> 01:21:48.999
I was standing, but PLLI,

01:21:49.000 --> 01:21:49.999
get up and stretch. Quickly!

01:21:50.000 --> 01:21:52.999
Oh, what's this? Looks like Hamin wants to
dance.

01:21:53.000 --> 01:22:01.999
Send dance emojis in the chat.

01:22:02.000 --> 01:22:04.999
What should I do for next year's birthday
stream?

01:22:05.000 --> 01:22:06.999
Already planning it.

01:22:07.000 --> 01:22:21.999
Power jegi-kicking?

01:22:22.000 --> 01:22:31.999
Ja, send those dance emojis, quick!

01:22:32.000 --> 01:22:38.999
Oh, here they come.

01:22:39.000 --> 01:22:42.999
Ja, I'm going to show you

01:22:43.000 --> 01:22:45.999
some dance challenges. I'll do each one
twice.

01:22:46.000 --> 01:22:47.999
The first run is a rehearsal

01:22:48.000 --> 01:22:50.999
where I just mark the moves. You know

01:22:51.000 --> 01:22:51.999
soundcheck at our concerts?

01:22:52.000 --> 01:22:53.999
Think of it like

01:22:54.000 --> 01:22:56.999
a soundcheck. It's not

01:22:57.000 --> 01:22:58.999
because I can't do the dance, or anything.

01:22:59.000 --> 01:23:00.999
You know? Just think of it as getting

01:23:01.000 --> 01:23:03.999
twice the cuteness. Ja, first challenge.

01:23:04.000 --> 01:23:29.999
Music, please.

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:51.999
Okay, here we go.

01:23:52.000 --> 01:23:53.999
Love you.

01:23:54.000 --> 01:23:56.999
Love you!

01:23:57.000 --> 01:23:59.999
How was “Teddy Bear”?

01:24:00.000 --> 01:24:00.999
Was it good?

01:24:01.000 --> 01:24:03.999
Let's go straight

01:24:04.000 --> 01:24:20.999
to the next challenge.

01:24:21.000 --> 01:24:23.999
I should move to a different spot. Okay.

01:24:24.000 --> 01:24:25.999
I'll make it cute.

01:24:26.000 --> 01:24:42.999
Cute and sexy.

01:24:43.000 --> 01:24:48.999
Love you!

01:24:49.000 --> 01:24:51.999
Hey, it went up! The cuteness meter went
up!

01:24:52.000 --> 01:24:59.999
Ja, straight into the next challenge.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:03.999
[Starts the cute chant]

01:25:04.000 --> 01:25:06.999
[Chant continues]

01:25:07.000 --> 01:25:09.999
[Chant continues]

01:25:10.000 --> 01:25:11.999
[Chant continues]

01:25:12.000 --> 01:25:17.999
[Chant continues]

01:25:18.000 --> 01:25:20.999
[Chant continues]

01:25:21.000 --> 01:25:21.999
[Chant trails off]

01:25:22.000 --> 01:25:23.999
Okay.

01:25:24.000 --> 01:25:25.999
I'll try

01:25:26.000 --> 01:25:31.999
to remember it.

01:25:32.000 --> 01:25:37.999
[Repeats the cute chant]

01:25:38.000 --> 01:25:40.999
[Chant continues]

01:25:41.000 --> 01:25:44.999
[Chant continues]

01:25:45.000 --> 01:25:50.999
[Chant continues]

01:25:51.000 --> 01:25:54.999
[Chant continues]

01:25:55.000 --> 01:26:00.999
[Chant concludes]

01:26:01.000 --> 01:26:02.999
How was it?

01:26:03.000 --> 01:26:06.999
Wow, my cuteness meter

01:26:07.000 --> 01:26:09.999
filled right up!

01:26:10.000 --> 01:26:10.999
Finally...

01:26:11.000 --> 01:26:14.999
Have I become a baby?

01:26:15.000 --> 01:26:16.999
Is that right?

01:26:17.000 --> 01:26:19.999
No! Now I'm going to become an oppa.

01:26:20.000 --> 01:26:22.999
Did cuteness go down one notch?

01:26:23.000 --> 01:26:25.999
Huh?

01:26:26.000 --> 01:26:27.999
Can you tell me why it dropped?

01:26:28.000 --> 01:26:31.999
Oh, was there still one notch left?

01:26:32.000 --> 01:26:33.999
So I have to look

01:26:34.000 --> 01:26:38.999
more like a baby. In that case...

01:26:39.000 --> 01:26:40.999
One more time.

01:26:41.000 --> 01:26:42.999
Yep.

01:26:43.000 --> 01:26:45.999
I'll show you again. One last

01:26:46.000 --> 01:26:50.999
cuteness challenge.

01:26:51.000 --> 01:26:55.999
I'll make it adorable.

01:26:56.000 --> 01:26:59.999
[Dance music]

01:27:00.000 --> 01:27:03.999
[Dance music continues]

01:27:04.000 --> 01:27:11.999
[Dance music continues]

01:27:12.000 --> 01:27:17.999
[Dance music continues]

01:27:18.000 --> 01:27:23.999
Love you!

01:27:24.000 --> 01:27:26.999
Wow!

01:27:27.000 --> 01:27:30.999
I've officially maxed out

01:27:31.000 --> 01:27:35.999
my cuteness. Now it's time

01:27:36.000 --> 01:27:39.999
to show you something cool.

01:27:40.000 --> 01:27:43.999
Hah!

01:27:44.000 --> 01:27:46.999
Don't get startled just yet.

01:27:47.000 --> 01:27:50.999
From this moment,

01:27:51.000 --> 01:27:53.999
you're under arrest.

01:27:54.000 --> 01:27:57.999
[Arrest-themed dance music]

01:27:58.000 --> 01:27:58.999
[Dance music continues]

01:27:59.000 --> 01:28:01.999
[Dance music continues]

01:28:02.000 --> 01:28:03.999
[Dance music continues]

01:28:04.000 --> 01:28:07.999
[Dance music continues]

01:28:08.000 --> 01:28:10.999
[Arrest chant]

01:28:11.000 --> 01:28:14.999
[Chant continues]

01:28:15.000 --> 01:28:17.999
[Chant continues]

01:28:18.000 --> 01:28:22.999
[Chant concludes]

01:28:23.000 --> 01:28:24.999
Ja, rehearsal's over, right?

01:28:25.000 --> 01:28:28.999
Let's do it for real.

01:28:29.000 --> 01:28:31.999
I'll shower you with cuteness.

01:28:32.000 --> 01:28:33.999
Wait, again.

01:28:34.000 --> 01:28:35.999
The suspect got away.

01:28:36.000 --> 01:28:54.999
I'm going after them.

01:28:55.000 --> 01:28:57.999
You're under arrest!

01:28:58.000 --> 01:29:01.999
You're under arrest!

01:29:02.000 --> 01:29:04.999
You're under a... cell arrest?

01:29:05.000 --> 01:29:07.999
Cell arrest!

01:29:08.000 --> 01:29:12.999
Freeze!

01:29:13.000 --> 01:29:15.999
I said freeze.

01:29:16.000 --> 01:29:17.999
You have the right to an attorney.

01:29:18.000 --> 01:29:19.999
I'll go again. You have the right to an
attorney,

01:29:20.000 --> 01:29:24.999
the right to remain silent,

01:29:25.000 --> 01:29:27.999
and the right to refuse to incriminate
yourself.

01:29:28.000 --> 01:29:34.999
And...

01:29:35.000 --> 01:29:37.999
I've been waiting for this.

01:29:38.000 --> 01:29:38.999
And just like that,

01:29:39.000 --> 01:29:41.999
I'm a step closer to being an oppa.

01:29:42.000 --> 01:29:47.999
On to the next challenge.

01:29:48.000 --> 01:30:14.999
[Dance music]

01:30:15.000 --> 01:30:31.999
[Dance track continues]

01:30:32.000 --> 01:30:34.999
Ja.

01:30:35.000 --> 01:30:36.999
It went up another notch?

01:30:37.000 --> 01:30:39.999
Ja, before

01:30:40.000 --> 01:30:42.999
I show you the last challenge,

01:30:43.000 --> 01:30:45.999
let's

01:30:46.000 --> 01:30:47.999
listen to the music and get PLLI

01:30:48.000 --> 01:30:52.999
a little more hyped.

01:30:53.000 --> 01:30:54.999
What kind of concept is it?

01:30:55.000 --> 01:31:18.999
Music, please.

01:31:19.000 --> 01:31:21.999
Okay.

01:31:22.000 --> 01:31:24.999
I finally heard what the challenge was.

01:31:25.000 --> 01:31:26.999
PLLI shouted it out for me,

01:31:27.000 --> 01:31:28.999
so now

01:31:29.000 --> 01:31:30.999
I'll show you

01:31:31.000 --> 01:31:32.999
how it's done.

01:31:33.000 --> 01:31:34.999
Music,

01:31:35.000 --> 01:32:00.999
please.

01:32:01.000 --> 01:32:07.999
Sorry, sorry.

01:32:08.000 --> 01:32:12.999
I think I threw my hip out doing that.

01:32:13.000 --> 01:32:16.999
Ah, now my oppa meter

01:32:17.000 --> 01:32:20.999
is maxed out too.

01:32:21.000 --> 01:32:22.999
Oh, we're back here! Ja,

01:32:23.000 --> 01:32:26.999
but the happiness meter isn't full yet.

01:32:27.000 --> 01:32:29.999
It's still pretty low.

01:32:30.000 --> 01:32:33.999
Ja, it should be about time

01:32:34.000 --> 01:32:35.999
for the members to call. Ja,

01:32:36.000 --> 01:32:38.999
what are they all doing right now?

01:32:39.000 --> 01:32:40.999
Which member

01:32:41.000 --> 01:32:44.999
is going to cheer Hamin up

01:32:45.000 --> 01:32:46.999
and make him happy?

01:32:47.000 --> 01:32:48.999
I'm looking for them.

01:32:49.000 --> 01:32:51.999
Oh, I think we're getting a call now.

01:32:52.000 --> 01:32:53.999
Let's see who it is.

01:32:54.000 --> 01:32:57.999
Where? Here? Over there? It's me...

01:32:58.000 --> 01:33:02.999
Hamin. It's okay.

01:33:03.000 --> 01:33:05.999
They're still getting ready.

01:33:06.000 --> 01:33:07.999
Whew.

01:33:08.000 --> 01:33:12.999
Ja. Oh, here it is. The chair's here.

01:33:13.000 --> 01:33:14.999
It's okay. Have some water. That went
well, right?

01:33:15.000 --> 01:33:17.999
Okay, grab some water, PLLI.

01:33:18.000 --> 01:33:26.999
Shall we toast? Cheers!

01:33:27.000 --> 01:33:28.999
You're asking what kind of voice this is?

01:33:29.000 --> 01:33:30.999
I don't know either. I really don't.

01:33:31.000 --> 01:33:32.999
Your way of talking changes as you go.

01:33:33.000 --> 01:33:34.999
You'll get it, PLLI,

01:33:35.000 --> 01:33:38.999
if you ever do a stream. Ja.

01:33:39.000 --> 01:33:40.999
Ja, looks like we're ready.

01:33:41.000 --> 01:33:42.999
Ja, let's see how the members

01:33:43.000 --> 01:33:45.999
will raise Hamin's happiness meter.

01:33:46.000 --> 01:33:47.999
Hello?

01:33:48.000 --> 01:33:48.999
Hello?

01:33:49.000 --> 01:33:50.999
Who's this?

01:33:51.000 --> 01:33:52.999
Yejun-hyung?

01:33:53.000 --> 01:33:55.999
Oh, Noah?

01:33:56.000 --> 01:33:58.999
It does sound pretty similar.

01:33:59.000 --> 01:34:00.999
Yeah.

01:34:01.000 --> 01:34:02.999
When you keep doing it...

01:34:03.000 --> 01:34:03.999
Maybe just...

01:34:04.000 --> 01:34:04.999
Hello?

01:34:05.000 --> 01:34:07.999
Maybe just... Yeah.

01:34:08.000 --> 01:34:08.999
Right.

01:34:09.000 --> 01:34:10.999
Why? — Ja, who is this?

01:34:11.000 --> 01:34:13.999
Ja, sorry, could you

01:34:14.000 --> 01:34:14.999
mute the livestream

01:34:15.000 --> 01:34:18.999
on your end? Hello?

01:34:19.000 --> 01:34:20.999
We're getting an echo.

01:34:21.000 --> 01:34:25.999
[Indistinct remark amid the echo]

01:34:26.000 --> 01:34:27.999
Are you on the subway or something?

01:34:28.000 --> 01:34:28.999
Hello?

01:34:29.000 --> 01:34:29.999
Yeah.

01:34:30.000 --> 01:34:30.999
Ah, yes, yes.

01:34:31.000 --> 01:34:32.999
Everything okay?

01:34:33.000 --> 01:34:34.999
Yes, I'm fine.

01:34:35.000 --> 01:34:36.999
Is it a good time to talk?

01:34:37.000 --> 01:34:37.999
Of course it is.

01:34:38.000 --> 01:34:38.999
Right, right.

01:34:39.000 --> 01:34:40.999
It's fine. Where's the birthday boy?

01:34:41.000 --> 01:34:43.999
I can call Hamin from anywhere.

01:34:44.000 --> 01:34:45.999
Right.

01:34:46.000 --> 01:34:47.999
Say hello, please.

01:34:48.000 --> 01:34:50.999
Hello!

01:34:51.000 --> 01:34:52.999
PLLI, it's Eunho. Eunho!

01:34:53.000 --> 01:34:54.999
Eunho-hyung is here! Applause!

01:34:55.000 --> 01:34:58.999
Sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry.

01:34:59.000 --> 01:34:59.999
What are you so sorry about?

01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:01.999
I enjoyed the dancing.

01:35:02.000 --> 01:35:02.999
Oh, you saw it?

01:35:03.000 --> 01:35:04.999
But the angle on that kick...

01:35:05.000 --> 01:35:06.999
— Yes? — I wanted a bit more from that
one.

01:35:07.000 --> 01:35:07.999
Right, right.

01:35:08.000 --> 01:35:09.999
Should've gone to 110 degrees.

01:35:10.000 --> 01:35:11.999
Right. Next time I get the chance,

01:35:12.000 --> 01:35:14.999
I'll show you the kick

01:35:15.000 --> 01:35:15.999
in person, Eunho.

01:35:16.000 --> 01:35:17.999
You're not aiming

01:35:18.000 --> 01:35:18.999
straight at my head, are you?

01:35:19.000 --> 01:35:19.999
Of course not. How could I

01:35:20.000 --> 01:35:23.999
do that to you, hyung?

01:35:24.000 --> 01:35:25.999
— Right. — Happy birthday!

01:35:26.000 --> 01:35:26.999
Thank you.

01:35:27.000 --> 01:35:28.999
So, how is it?

01:35:29.000 --> 01:35:31.999
What? How am I feeling?

01:35:32.000 --> 01:35:32.999
How are you feeling?

01:35:33.000 --> 01:35:34.999
Ja, my oppa meter

01:35:35.000 --> 01:35:37.999
and cuteness meter are way up, which is
great,

01:35:38.000 --> 01:35:39.999
but happiness isn't full yet.

01:35:40.000 --> 01:35:42.999
Oh. Ah, that's why

01:35:43.000 --> 01:35:43.999
I called.

01:35:44.000 --> 01:35:44.999
Am I a baby or an oppa?

01:35:45.000 --> 01:35:46.999
Can you decide for me,

01:35:47.000 --> 01:35:47.999
Eunho.

01:35:48.000 --> 01:35:49.999
Ah, not sure if you're a baby

01:35:50.000 --> 01:35:50.999
or an oppa.

01:35:51.000 --> 01:35:52.999
Right.

01:35:53.000 --> 01:35:57.999
You're a T, Hamin, aren't you?

01:35:58.000 --> 01:36:00.999
Can we not make the stream boring?

01:36:01.000 --> 01:36:02.999
Ja, we're in year four of doing this,

01:36:03.000 --> 01:36:04.999
everyone. Yes, yes.

01:36:05.000 --> 01:36:07.999
Right.

01:36:08.000 --> 01:36:10.999
Baby or oppa: don't give me

01:36:11.000 --> 01:36:12.999
such a babyish answer.

01:36:13.000 --> 01:36:15.999
I'll ask again, like a pro.

01:36:16.000 --> 01:36:17.999
— Right, right.

01:36:18.000 --> 01:36:20.999
My oppa meter and my cuteness meter

01:36:21.000 --> 01:36:23.999
are both full. I can't tell

01:36:24.000 --> 01:36:24.999
whether I'm a baby or an oppa.

01:36:25.000 --> 01:36:28.999
Well, Hamin, let's see...

01:36:29.000 --> 01:36:32.999
Both meters are full, but

01:36:33.000 --> 01:36:34.999
watching your dance challenges today...

01:36:35.000 --> 01:36:37.999
Right, it's hard

01:36:38.000 --> 01:36:41.999
to pick a winner. But for me,

01:36:42.000 --> 01:36:46.999
that one...

01:36:47.000 --> 01:36:48.999
It was just so cool.

01:36:49.000 --> 01:36:51.999
You were shining like a neon sign.

01:36:52.000 --> 01:36:53.999
I'll go with oppa.

01:36:54.000 --> 01:36:55.999
Oh, oppa! Excellent. Applause, please.

01:36:56.000 --> 01:36:57.999
Nice, nice.

01:36:58.000 --> 01:36:59.999
Thank you.

01:37:00.000 --> 01:37:01.999
Right. There was one bit where

01:37:02.000 --> 01:37:03.999
you suddenly spoke a foreign language,
hyung,

01:37:04.000 --> 01:37:06.999
and I couldn't translate a few parts.

01:37:07.000 --> 01:37:08.999
When did I speak a foreign language?

01:37:09.000 --> 01:37:09.999
Didn't you go “yah, hah, ah,”

01:37:10.000 --> 01:37:10.999
that kind of thing?

01:37:11.000 --> 01:37:14.999
Oh, when you were dancing earlier.

01:37:15.000 --> 01:37:16.999
Yeah, that part.

01:37:17.000 --> 01:37:18.999
Oh, you were imitating that!

01:37:19.000 --> 01:37:20.999
Wow.

01:37:21.000 --> 01:37:22.999
I see.

01:37:23.000 --> 01:37:26.999
You're really saving your voice, huh?

01:37:27.000 --> 01:37:29.999
And that dance where you went, “Sorry,
sorry.”

01:37:30.000 --> 01:37:31.999
You did it so well. It was so cool.

01:37:32.000 --> 01:37:32.999
Yeah.

01:37:33.000 --> 01:37:34.999
That's why I picked oppa.

01:37:35.000 --> 01:37:38.999
Oh, you picked oppa. If you had

01:37:39.000 --> 01:37:41.999
one line to say to me, what would it be?

01:37:42.000 --> 01:37:43.999
What message would you give me?

01:37:44.000 --> 01:37:45.999
Well, first of all,

01:37:46.000 --> 01:37:48.999
happy birthday.

01:37:49.000 --> 01:37:49.999
— Thanks. — That's the first thing.

01:37:50.000 --> 01:37:50.999
Right.

01:37:51.000 --> 01:37:53.999
And you prepared so much.

01:37:54.000 --> 01:37:56.999
It went way beyond

01:37:57.000 --> 01:37:57.999
what I was expecting.

01:37:58.000 --> 01:38:00.999
Wow. What did you think

01:38:01.000 --> 01:38:02.999
when you saw it?

01:38:03.000 --> 01:38:04.999
It was amazing. I mean,

01:38:05.000 --> 01:38:06.999
I've been watching since the start.

01:38:07.000 --> 01:38:10.999
Normally, with the other hyungs'

01:38:11.000 --> 01:38:14.999
birthday streams,

01:38:15.000 --> 01:38:16.999
I watch for ten minutes to get the gist,

01:38:17.000 --> 01:38:18.999
then take a break in the middle.

01:38:19.000 --> 01:38:20.999
Twenty, thirty minutes off,

01:38:21.000 --> 01:38:21.999
then I tune back in

01:38:22.000 --> 01:38:22.999
around call time.

01:38:23.000 --> 01:38:25.999
Wow, you're honest.

01:38:26.000 --> 01:38:28.999
But for your stream, Hamin,

01:38:29.000 --> 01:38:30.999
I had it on before it even started

01:38:31.000 --> 01:38:31.999
and kept watching.

01:38:32.000 --> 01:38:32.999
Really?

01:38:33.000 --> 01:38:33.999
Of course!

01:38:34.000 --> 01:38:35.999
Wow. The affection meter won't go higher.

01:38:36.000 --> 01:38:38.999
I mean, happiness should be

01:38:39.000 --> 01:38:40.999
going up after that.

01:38:41.000 --> 01:38:42.999
Compared to how I feel,

01:38:43.000 --> 01:38:43.999
that meter's still too low.

01:38:44.000 --> 01:38:45.999
Well, in my heart,

01:38:46.000 --> 01:38:47.999
the happiness meter is fully charged.

01:38:48.000 --> 01:38:50.999
Wow.

01:38:51.000 --> 01:38:51.999
Thank you. I'm honored.

01:38:52.000 --> 01:38:53.999
Eunho, moments like this

01:38:54.000 --> 01:38:54.999
make me think you're a genius.

01:38:55.000 --> 01:38:56.999
Oh, how many years have I been

01:38:57.000 --> 01:38:57.999
doing this now?

01:38:58.000 --> 01:38:59.999
I learned it from you, Hamin.

01:39:00.000 --> 01:39:01.999
No, but really, Eunho,

01:39:02.000 --> 01:39:02.999
you're a genius.

01:39:03.000 --> 01:39:05.999
Good grief, what's gotten into you

01:39:06.000 --> 01:39:07.999
all of a sudden?

01:39:08.000 --> 01:39:09.999
Anyway, ja, today...

01:39:10.000 --> 01:39:10.999
No, Eunho.

01:39:11.000 --> 01:39:13.999
— Yes? — I mean it. A genius.

01:39:14.000 --> 01:39:19.999
Well, uh...

01:39:20.000 --> 01:39:21.999
I turned on the TV,

01:39:22.000 --> 01:39:24.999
but I'd stopped watching for a moment

01:39:25.000 --> 01:39:25.999
to make the call.

01:39:26.000 --> 01:39:27.999
Wow, an actual genius.

01:39:28.000 --> 01:39:29.999
There's something

01:39:30.000 --> 01:39:30.999
I want to say, though.

01:39:31.000 --> 01:39:32.999
Oh, what is it?

01:39:33.000 --> 01:39:35.999
Seeing all the martial arts stuff

01:39:36.000 --> 01:39:37.999
you prepared today...

01:39:38.000 --> 01:39:40.999
— Yeah? — I just can't leave without
saying this:

01:39:41.000 --> 01:39:43.999
Hamin, you really are a genius.

01:39:44.000 --> 01:39:47.999
Love you. — A round of applause for Eunho!

01:39:48.000 --> 01:39:50.999
Seriously, the Tekken thing today...

01:39:51.000 --> 01:39:53.999
How'd you think of going inside the game?

01:39:54.000 --> 01:39:54.999
Seriously, you're a genius.

01:39:55.000 --> 01:39:56.999
I just popped in and came back out.

01:39:57.000 --> 01:39:58.999
Took a quick look, that's all.

01:39:59.000 --> 01:40:02.999
You're a genius, seriously.

01:40:03.000 --> 01:40:04.999
At this point, Eunho-hyung may as well

01:40:05.000 --> 01:40:08.999
have given birth to me.

01:40:09.000 --> 01:40:10.999
Ah, this birthday stream is fun.

01:40:11.000 --> 01:40:12.999
These calls are always so much fun.

01:40:13.000 --> 01:40:13.999
Right, right.

01:40:14.000 --> 01:40:17.999
And all the stuff you put together
today...

01:40:18.000 --> 01:40:19.999
Did you join the production team, Hamin?

01:40:20.000 --> 01:40:21.999
I've got one foot in the door.

01:40:22.000 --> 01:40:23.999
You packed so much into this.

01:40:24.000 --> 01:40:25.999
Right, right.

01:40:26.000 --> 01:40:27.999
Oh, and I enjoyed

01:40:28.000 --> 01:40:29.999
the rap, too.

01:40:30.000 --> 01:40:31.999
I came up with a little something.

01:40:32.000 --> 01:40:33.999
You know, about deciding what to eat?

01:40:34.000 --> 01:40:36.999
Something spicy, sweet

01:40:37.000 --> 01:40:37.999
or salty.

01:40:38.000 --> 01:40:38.999
You with Baedal Minjok?

01:40:39.000 --> 01:40:40.999
No, no. That's what you were doing

01:40:41.000 --> 01:40:41.999
in the rap.

01:40:42.000 --> 01:40:43.999
Oh, “Spicy, Salty, Sweet.”

01:40:44.000 --> 01:40:47.999
Oh, salty, not savory.

01:40:48.000 --> 01:40:48.999
I got that mixed up.

01:40:49.000 --> 01:40:52.999
Right. I bet

01:40:53.000 --> 01:40:54.999
you'd be good at ordering in rap,

01:40:55.000 --> 01:40:57.999
Eunho. — Ah, sure. Next time,

01:40:58.000 --> 01:40:58.999
if I get a chance to show you,

01:40:59.000 --> 01:40:59.999
I'll do a food rap.

01:41:00.000 --> 01:41:01.999
Oh, next time you get a chance,

01:41:02.000 --> 01:41:03.999
let's do a food rap together.

01:41:04.000 --> 01:41:05.999
Sounds good.

01:41:06.000 --> 01:41:07.999
Today's stream feels like...

01:41:08.000 --> 01:41:12.999
Oh, the DJ! This party's so fun.

01:41:13.000 --> 01:41:15.999
Eunho, it's time for us to part.

01:41:16.000 --> 01:41:18.999
The point of this call was to keep

01:41:19.000 --> 01:41:21.999
Hamin's energy where it is

01:41:22.000 --> 01:41:23.999
and give it a little boost.

01:41:24.000 --> 01:41:24.999
That's why I called today.

01:41:25.000 --> 01:41:28.999
Whenever I call on a birthday stream,

01:41:29.000 --> 01:41:33.999
I have a sweet concept, a serious one,

01:41:34.000 --> 01:41:35.999
a charismatic one,

01:41:36.000 --> 01:41:36.999
and...

01:41:37.000 --> 01:41:38.999
Then there's the sexy concept.

01:41:39.000 --> 01:41:40.999
Right. For that, I drop my voice

01:41:41.000 --> 01:41:43.999
and throw in some English.

01:41:44.000 --> 01:41:45.999
But you told me not to speak English
today,

01:41:46.000 --> 01:41:47.999
Hamin, so

01:41:48.000 --> 01:41:49.999
I'm skipping sexy this time.

01:41:50.000 --> 01:41:50.999
Understood.

01:41:51.000 --> 01:41:53.999
Anyway, I shouldn't keep

01:41:54.000 --> 01:41:55.999
you on the phone too long.

01:41:56.000 --> 01:41:57.999
No, Eunho, I love your voice.

01:41:58.000 --> 01:41:59.999
But we are a little pressed for time.

01:42:00.000 --> 01:42:00.999
I know. I know exactly

01:42:01.000 --> 01:42:02.999
how much time

01:42:03.000 --> 01:42:05.999
I've been given. I'm a professional...

01:42:06.000 --> 01:42:06.999
Just kidding.

01:42:07.000 --> 01:42:07.999
I know I've got to hang up

01:42:08.000 --> 01:42:11.999
before the fifty-minute mark.

01:42:12.000 --> 01:42:12.999
No, you don't.

01:42:13.000 --> 01:42:14.999
That way Noah-hyung

01:42:15.000 --> 01:42:15.999
can do a short call, probably.

01:42:16.000 --> 01:42:16.999
Hmm.

01:42:17.000 --> 01:42:17.999
Eunho, something I wanted

01:42:18.000 --> 01:42:20.999
to ask you...

01:42:21.000 --> 01:42:22.999
Is your throat doing okay?

01:42:23.000 --> 01:42:25.999
I already told PLLI about it.

01:42:26.000 --> 01:42:28.999
Oh, did you? — Yeah, hepatitis A... ah,

01:42:29.000 --> 01:42:32.999
not hepatitis A. Influenza A.

01:42:33.000 --> 01:42:34.999
That's what I told them.

01:42:35.000 --> 01:42:36.999
Oh, you told them.

01:42:37.000 --> 01:42:39.999
Yeah, but really,

01:42:40.000 --> 01:42:42.999
I'm fine. It's not like I passed out.

01:42:43.000 --> 01:42:44.999
I didn't pass out or anything.

01:42:45.000 --> 01:42:45.999
It's manageable.

01:42:46.000 --> 01:42:47.999
I told them because I was okay,

01:42:48.000 --> 01:42:49.999
and I told them not to worry.

01:42:50.000 --> 01:42:51.999
Hamin, you should

01:42:52.000 --> 01:42:52.999
take care too.

01:42:53.000 --> 01:42:54.999
Right. Eunho, even in the chat

01:42:55.000 --> 01:42:55.999
PLLI are worried about you

01:42:56.000 --> 01:42:56.999
right now.

01:42:57.000 --> 01:42:58.999
Actually, Hamin,

01:42:59.000 --> 01:42:59.999
I'm worried about you too.

01:43:00.000 --> 01:43:01.999
I saw you yesterday...

01:43:02.000 --> 01:43:03.999
Yeah. No, Hamin,

01:43:04.000 --> 01:43:07.999
don't get sick. Did he tell you, everyone?

01:43:08.000 --> 01:43:10.999
Hamin was so determined to do well.

01:43:11.000 --> 01:43:12.999
I'm not saying he was sick,

01:43:13.000 --> 01:43:13.999
but he got an IV for energy.

01:43:14.000 --> 01:43:16.999
Oh, I didn't tell them that.

01:43:17.000 --> 01:43:19.999
I brought it up on purpose, but

01:43:20.000 --> 01:43:20.999
was I not supposed to?

01:43:21.000 --> 01:43:22.999
No, no. I mean,

01:43:23.000 --> 01:43:24.999
it wasn't that I was sick.

01:43:25.000 --> 01:43:26.999
My throat was in really bad shape today,

01:43:27.000 --> 01:43:27.999
so that's why I got it.

01:43:28.000 --> 01:43:29.999
Oh, was it?

01:43:30.000 --> 01:43:32.999
But I was surprised.

01:43:33.000 --> 01:43:35.999
From backstage it was like, “Hey, Hamin,
come out!”

01:43:36.000 --> 01:43:36.999
And I was like, “Wait, what?”

01:43:37.000 --> 01:43:38.999
Right. I thought you might tell them

01:43:39.000 --> 01:43:39.999
during your TMI earlier.

01:43:40.000 --> 01:43:42.999
I was watching to see if you would.

01:43:43.000 --> 01:43:44.999
I didn't bring it up because

01:43:45.000 --> 01:43:47.999
I didn't want anyone to worry.

01:43:48.000 --> 01:43:50.999
I thought about whether to say it, too.

01:43:51.000 --> 01:43:53.999
But it wasn't anything

01:43:54.000 --> 01:43:55.999
PLLI needed to worry about. — Right.

01:43:56.000 --> 01:43:56.999
That's right.

01:43:57.000 --> 01:43:59.999
I just wanted PLLI to know

01:44:00.000 --> 01:44:01.999
how hard Hamin worked on the stream.

01:44:02.000 --> 01:44:04.999
All that preparation behind the scenes

01:44:05.000 --> 01:44:06.999
to get his energy up

01:44:07.000 --> 01:44:08.999
and feel ready.

01:44:09.000 --> 01:44:09.999
That's why I brought it up.

01:44:10.000 --> 01:44:11.999
Ah, thank you

01:44:12.000 --> 01:44:12.999
for thinking of me.

01:44:13.000 --> 01:44:13.999
Good kitty. Proud of you.

01:44:14.000 --> 01:44:15.999
Good kitty, yes.

01:44:16.000 --> 01:44:18.999
Anyway, your energy's great today.

01:44:19.000 --> 01:44:19.999
Really good.

01:44:20.000 --> 01:44:20.999
Right, right.

01:44:21.000 --> 01:44:22.999
I'll keep watching

01:44:23.000 --> 01:44:24.999
all the way to the end.

01:44:25.000 --> 01:44:27.999
Great. Eunho, rest your voice,

01:44:28.000 --> 01:44:28.999
and tomorrow let's

01:44:29.000 --> 01:44:31.999
see each other smiling. — Sounds good.

01:44:32.000 --> 01:44:32.999
And happy birthday

01:44:33.000 --> 01:44:34.999
again.

01:44:35.000 --> 01:44:36.999
Say goodbye to PLLI, please.

01:44:37.000 --> 01:44:41.999
PLLI, have a great time with Hamin.

01:44:42.000 --> 01:44:44.999
And wish him

01:44:45.000 --> 01:44:46.999
a very happy birthday!

01:44:47.000 --> 01:44:47.999
Thank you.

01:44:48.000 --> 01:44:49.999
And don't laugh.

01:44:50.000 --> 01:44:51.999
Thank you! That was Eunho.

01:44:52.000 --> 01:44:53.999
Give him a round of applause.

01:44:54.000 --> 01:44:57.999
— Nice! — Love you. Rest your throat.

01:44:58.000 --> 01:45:02.999
Yeah, I'm going running. Just kidding.

01:45:03.000 --> 01:45:04.999
Ja, that was our call

01:45:05.000 --> 01:45:07.999
with Eunho-hyung. Now I think

01:45:08.000 --> 01:45:09.999
Noah-hyung is the only one left.

01:45:10.000 --> 01:45:12.999
Talking with Eunho-hyung reminded me:

01:45:13.000 --> 01:45:15.999
the members are all very careful

01:45:16.000 --> 01:45:17.999
about taking care of their health.

01:45:18.000 --> 01:45:19.999
So you don't have to worry too much.

01:45:20.000 --> 01:45:21.999
At the slightest sign of feeling unwell,

01:45:22.000 --> 01:45:24.999
we go straight to the doctor

01:45:25.000 --> 01:45:27.999
and take care of it

01:45:28.000 --> 01:45:30.999
so we can recover. That way

01:45:31.000 --> 01:45:32.999
we can give a hundred percent onstage

01:45:33.000 --> 01:45:35.999
and enjoy it. So please don't worry.

01:45:36.000 --> 01:45:36.999
I wasn't trying to hide it.

01:45:37.000 --> 01:45:39.999
I just didn't want you

01:45:40.000 --> 01:45:42.999
to get the wrong idea and worry.

01:45:43.000 --> 01:45:45.999
Anyway, I'm fine now,

01:45:46.000 --> 01:45:47.999
so don't worry.

01:45:48.000 --> 01:45:55.999
Ja, a sip of water.

01:45:56.000 --> 01:45:59.999
Ja, “the princess is coming.”

01:46:00.000 --> 01:46:01.999
The princess!

01:46:02.000 --> 01:46:04.999
Ja, Noah. It's about time

01:46:05.000 --> 01:46:07.999
for Noah to call.

01:46:08.000 --> 01:46:09.999
Any minute, really.

01:46:10.000 --> 01:46:11.999
Not yet.

01:46:12.000 --> 01:46:15.999
Ja, Noah's... uh...

01:46:16.000 --> 01:46:18.999
That's fine. Actually, I like

01:46:19.000 --> 01:46:20.999
having time to talk to PLLI like this.

01:46:21.000 --> 01:46:22.999
I love getting to chat face-to-face.

01:46:23.000 --> 01:46:24.999
It feels different, doesn't it?

01:46:25.000 --> 01:46:27.999
Weverse is great, and so is Bubble.

01:46:28.000 --> 01:46:30.999
But when we're face-to-face, you can

01:46:31.000 --> 01:46:34.999
pick up more from gestures and
expressions.

01:46:35.000 --> 01:46:38.999
That's how it feels to me. Anyway,

01:46:39.000 --> 01:46:39.999
as we were saying earlier,

01:46:40.000 --> 01:46:42.999
if there's anything

01:46:43.000 --> 01:46:44.999
you're curious about, we could

01:46:45.000 --> 01:46:49.999
talk about it here.

01:46:50.000 --> 01:46:51.999
Ja, leave a few short questions

01:46:52.000 --> 01:46:57.999
in the chat.

01:46:58.000 --> 01:46:59.999
Uh...

01:47:00.000 --> 01:47:02.999
“Where'd Noah go?” You're looking

01:47:03.000 --> 01:47:05.999
for him.

01:47:06.000 --> 01:47:08.999
Someone wants the story of how

01:47:09.000 --> 01:47:10.999
we decided the filming order.

01:47:11.000 --> 01:47:12.999
Well, we film a lot,

01:47:13.000 --> 01:47:15.999
but every shoot's different.

01:47:16.000 --> 01:47:17.999
Sometimes we finish up

01:47:18.000 --> 01:47:19.999
with individual shots. On those days,

01:47:20.000 --> 01:47:22.999
we go in order, so

01:47:23.000 --> 01:47:25.999
whoever shoots first can go home first.

01:47:26.000 --> 01:47:27.999
When that happens,

01:47:28.000 --> 01:47:30.999
the order really matters.

01:47:31.000 --> 01:47:32.999
But the hyungs are so sweet.

01:47:33.000 --> 01:47:34.999
They don't make the youngest go last.

01:47:35.000 --> 01:47:36.999
Instead, it's “Ja, how should we decide?”

01:47:37.000 --> 01:47:38.999
So I'd suggest,

01:47:39.000 --> 01:47:41.999
“Rock-paper-scissors? A game?”

01:47:42.000 --> 01:47:43.999
Since everyone was waiting,

01:47:44.000 --> 01:47:45.999
we quickly did rock-paper-scissors.

01:47:46.000 --> 01:47:47.999
Bamby got lucky and took first.

01:47:48.000 --> 01:47:49.999
For second, we played the take-one-away
version.

01:47:50.000 --> 01:47:50.999
Take one away. You know it?

01:47:51.000 --> 01:47:53.999
Then Yejun-hyung

01:47:54.000 --> 01:47:56.999
came in second. From third place on,

01:47:57.000 --> 01:47:59.999
we switched to a different game.

01:48:00.000 --> 01:48:02.999
We pushed a box up against the wall.

01:48:03.000 --> 01:48:05.999
Like darts, we'd stand right back

01:48:06.000 --> 01:48:08.999
with a shoulder against the wall and
throw,

01:48:09.000 --> 01:48:10.999
trying to land it on top of the box.

01:48:11.000 --> 01:48:13.999
It bounced around a lot,

01:48:14.000 --> 01:48:16.999
and Eunho-hyung got lucky and took third.

01:48:17.000 --> 01:48:21.999
That left me and Noah-hyung.

01:48:22.000 --> 01:48:24.999
Well, honestly, no contest at that point.

01:48:25.000 --> 01:48:27.999
Look, with Noah-hyung, it went like
this...

01:48:28.000 --> 01:48:28.999
Just like throwing a dart.

01:48:29.000 --> 01:48:30.999
Whoosh!

01:48:31.000 --> 01:48:32.999
You throw it, and if it falls,

01:48:33.000 --> 01:48:34.999
you're out. Mine went up and...

01:48:35.000 --> 01:48:38.999
landed right on top. So now you're asking

01:48:39.000 --> 01:48:41.999
me to reenact how I leapfrogged
Noah-hyung?

01:48:42.000 --> 01:48:44.999
I didn't literally

01:48:45.000 --> 01:48:47.999
jump over Noah-hyung. I just went

01:48:48.000 --> 01:48:50.999
like this. You know the “Kakurenbo” stage?

01:48:51.000 --> 01:48:53.999
The jump when we come out?

01:48:54.000 --> 01:48:56.999
Now it doesn't feel right if I skip it.

01:48:57.000 --> 01:48:58.999
What am I supposed to do?

01:48:59.000 --> 01:49:02.999
I have to jump whenever “Kakurenbo” plays.

01:49:03.000 --> 01:49:03.999
It's rubbing off

01:49:04.000 --> 01:49:05.999
on the hyungs too.

01:49:06.000 --> 01:49:07.999
I do it because

01:49:08.000 --> 01:49:10.999
it feels so good.

01:49:11.000 --> 01:49:11.999
It'd be fun if PLLI jumped

01:49:12.000 --> 01:49:13.999
along while watching us perform,

01:49:14.000 --> 01:49:16.999
but someone might get hurt. That's just

01:49:17.000 --> 01:49:18.999
a little wish of mine.

01:49:19.000 --> 01:49:22.999
Ja, anyway...

01:49:23.000 --> 01:49:25.999
I also got recommendations for detergent,

01:49:26.000 --> 01:49:28.999
fabric softener and a scent booster,

01:49:29.000 --> 01:49:29.999
so PLLI and I can match.

01:49:30.000 --> 01:49:33.999
It was Cotton Candy, right?

01:49:34.000 --> 01:49:36.999
I picked that one. What do you think?

01:49:37.000 --> 01:49:40.999
I'm happy with it. I really like it.

01:49:41.000 --> 01:49:45.999
It's a different kind of scent from
before.

01:49:46.000 --> 01:49:48.999
I think it's nice,

01:49:49.000 --> 01:49:51.999
and it suits the weather now.

01:49:52.000 --> 01:49:54.999
It was a good recommendation. I wonder

01:49:55.000 --> 01:49:59.999
if PLLI feel the same way.

01:50:00.000 --> 01:50:04.999
If you do...

01:50:05.000 --> 01:50:05.999
PLLI?

01:50:06.000 --> 01:50:08.999
Nice, right? Smells good? It's the same

01:50:09.000 --> 01:50:11.999
scent I'm using. I'll use it for now,

01:50:12.000 --> 01:50:13.999
and then in summer...

01:50:14.000 --> 01:50:15.999
Maybe we could switch when the seasons
change.

01:50:16.000 --> 01:50:19.999
We could pick a summery scent

01:50:20.000 --> 01:50:23.999
and use the same fabric softener,
detergent

01:50:24.000 --> 01:50:27.999
or whatever. I think that'd be lovely.

01:50:28.000 --> 01:50:29.999
As time goes on,

01:50:30.000 --> 01:50:32.999
PLLI and I have more things that match,

01:50:33.000 --> 01:50:35.999
and we get to know each other better.

01:50:36.000 --> 01:50:38.999
That's what makes me so happy lately.

01:50:39.000 --> 01:50:40.999
That's my happiness meter. It's really...

01:50:41.000 --> 01:50:43.999
Come on, go up. There it is!

01:50:44.000 --> 01:50:46.999
You're so sweet. And the Dduks

01:50:47.000 --> 01:50:47.999
are sweet too.

01:50:48.000 --> 01:50:52.999
The Dduks must be laughing right now.

01:50:53.000 --> 01:50:54.999
Someone's curious about perfume.

01:50:55.000 --> 01:50:57.999
I haven't been wearing it much lately.

01:50:58.000 --> 01:51:00.999
As far as perfume goes, I'd probably

01:51:01.000 --> 01:51:02.999
still recommend the same one as before.

01:51:03.000 --> 01:51:05.999
I haven't bought any lately, but if I find

01:51:06.000 --> 01:51:07.999
a good one,

01:51:08.000 --> 01:51:10.999
I'll recommend it to you.

01:51:11.000 --> 01:51:14.999
So where's Noah-hyung going?

01:51:15.000 --> 01:51:18.999
Oh, really? Come on, calling

01:51:19.000 --> 01:51:22.999
at ten?

01:51:23.000 --> 01:51:24.999
Noah-hyung will have to start

01:51:25.000 --> 01:51:27.999
with zero affection points.

01:51:28.000 --> 01:51:29.999
Ja, you're asking how I'm feeling?

01:51:30.000 --> 01:51:34.999
I feel great. Like I could fly.

01:51:35.000 --> 01:51:38.999
Hmm. Here's another question.

01:51:39.000 --> 01:51:41.999
Was it hard preparing the challenges?

01:51:42.000 --> 01:51:46.999
It wasn't hard exactly.

01:51:47.000 --> 01:51:48.999
Everyone defines hard differently.

01:51:49.000 --> 01:51:54.999
What matters is whether

01:51:55.000 --> 01:51:56.999
there's something worthwhile in it.

01:51:57.000 --> 01:51:59.999
There's being physically or mentally

01:52:00.000 --> 01:52:02.999
exhausted for nothing, and then there's

01:52:03.000 --> 01:52:04.999
getting to see PLLI happy

01:52:05.000 --> 01:52:07.999
with what you show them. That kind of hard

01:52:08.000 --> 01:52:10.999
is worth it. That's how it feels to me.

01:52:11.000 --> 01:52:12.999
Of course, when I prepare a challenge,

01:52:13.000 --> 01:52:14.999
I have to memorize the choreography.

01:52:15.000 --> 01:52:17.999
That takes time and effort.

01:52:18.000 --> 01:52:20.999
But it isn't that hard.

01:52:21.000 --> 01:52:24.999
Mostly I just wonder,

01:52:25.000 --> 01:52:27.999
“How do I put my own spin on this?”

01:52:28.000 --> 01:52:29.999
That's the only thing

01:52:30.000 --> 01:52:33.999
I worry about, really.

01:52:34.000 --> 01:52:36.999
How did I book Caligo?

01:52:37.000 --> 01:52:39.999
I bumped into him.

01:52:40.000 --> 01:52:43.999
I just asked if he was free.

01:52:44.000 --> 01:52:47.999
It was a chance encounter.

01:52:48.000 --> 01:52:49.999
Caligo and I are actually quite close.

01:52:50.000 --> 01:52:52.999
Yeah.

01:52:53.000 --> 01:52:55.999
He's always

01:52:56.000 --> 01:52:59.999
giving it his all as a Caligo PLLI.

01:53:00.000 --> 01:53:02.999
Always doing his best.

01:53:03.000 --> 01:53:05.999
Apparently, anyway.

01:53:06.000 --> 01:53:07.999
Oh...

01:53:08.000 --> 01:53:12.999
I'm reading the next question.

01:53:13.000 --> 01:53:13.999
My favorite

01:53:14.000 --> 01:53:20.999
PLAVE song? You're asking me?

01:53:21.000 --> 01:53:25.999
They're all good, honestly.

01:53:26.000 --> 01:53:27.999
That's so hard.

01:53:28.000 --> 01:53:33.999
But I really love “Star Trace.”

01:53:34.000 --> 01:53:37.999
I like them all, though.

01:53:38.000 --> 01:53:41.999
“Star Trace,” for now.

01:53:42.000 --> 01:53:45.999
I don't think I've

01:53:46.000 --> 01:53:47.999
gotten tired of it yet.

01:53:48.000 --> 01:53:51.999
Normally, after practicing over and over,

01:53:52.000 --> 01:53:54.999
listening, choreographing,

01:53:55.000 --> 01:53:57.999
and doing it at concerts, I start to think

01:53:58.000 --> 01:53:59.999
I'd like to hear something else.

01:54:00.000 --> 01:54:01.999
I haven't reached that point yet.

01:54:02.000 --> 01:54:03.999
Hmm.

01:54:04.000 --> 01:54:08.999
You know what I mean, right?

01:54:09.000 --> 01:54:10.999
They're all great, really.

01:54:11.000 --> 01:54:12.999
PLLI, you know...

01:54:13.000 --> 01:54:14.999
When winter comes,

01:54:15.000 --> 01:54:19.999
we've got to listen to “Merry PLLIstmas,”
too.

01:54:20.000 --> 01:54:23.999
Ah, it smells like winter now.

01:54:24.000 --> 01:54:26.999
It makes me realize the year's nearly
over.

01:54:27.000 --> 01:54:30.999
To me, this felt like

01:54:31.000 --> 01:54:33.999
the fastest year yet.

01:54:34.000 --> 01:54:37.999
Seriously.

01:54:38.000 --> 01:54:39.999
Why is that?

01:54:40.000 --> 01:54:43.999
But it might also be the year

01:54:44.000 --> 01:54:47.999
with the most memories.

01:54:48.000 --> 01:54:50.999
And I did that little thing...

01:54:51.000 --> 01:54:51.999
A little series

01:54:52.000 --> 01:54:55.999
on Weverse, where on the first of every
month

01:54:56.000 --> 01:54:58.999
